BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages were separated by a vast desert. Each village had a single well) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    , but a strange magic bound them: any water poured into one well would triple before flowing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (     into the other village's well.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (  The villages took turns as the Giver. When the First Village poured water, it flowed threefold) Tj ET
