BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  At first, fear ruled. The First Village sent little, thinking, "What if they keep it all?" Rec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    eiving only a trickle, the Second Village returned nothing. Both grew thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  Then came the season of drought. The First Village's elder said, "We perish either way. Let us) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (     pour generously and trust." They sent their full bucket. The Second Village received three ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    buckets-abundance! ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  Grateful and moved by such trust, they sent back two buckets. The First Village now had more t) Tj ET
