BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Two Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  In the beginning, the gods placed two villages on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each vill) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    age had a sacred spring that produced five measures of water daily-enough to survive, but no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    t to flourish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  The gods whispered a secret to the villages: "If water from your spring crosses the valley, it) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (     shall triple before reaching the other side.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  The first village, filled with fear, hoarded their water. They survived, but their fields rema) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    ined dust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  The second village chose differently. They sent their water across the valley in clay vessels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (     When it arrived, it had become fifteen measures. The receiving village saw this gift and un) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    derstood-they returned half, sending seven measures back, which tripled to twenty-one.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  Soon both villages sent water freely. The valley bloomed green. Children laughed in gardens. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    he springs themselves grew stronger, as if rewarded by the gods for the villages' wisdom.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  One elder explained to her grandchildren: "Abundance is born from trust. When we clutch our fi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    ve measures close, we die slowly with full hands. But when we release them into the crossing) Tj ET
