BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  In ancient times, the River flowed down from the mountains, carrying precious water. Each seas) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    on, the River faced a choice: hold its waters close, or send them flowing to the Fields belo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    w.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  The River learned that when it gave freely, the waters multiplied threefold across the thirsty) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (     earth. The Fields would flourish with crops and flowers, creating abundance where there had) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (     been scarcity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  But the River could not survive on generosity alone. It depended on the Fields to return what ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    was needed-not all that was received, but enough to sustain the flow for seasons to come.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  When the Fields were grateful and returned fairly, the cycle continued: the River gave, the wa) Tj ET
