BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    hat either could achieve alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  Yet when the Fields grew selfish, keeping all they received, the River would run dry in future) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (     seasons. And when the River held back in fear, the Fields withered, and there was nothing t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    o return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  The wise understood: the greatest abundance flows when the River trusts enough to give, and th) Tj ET
