BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of Giving and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (         River of Return. Each was fed by a different mountain spring, and neither alone could b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        ring life to the land.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      The River of Giving was generous but weak, trickling through the dust. When it offered its) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (         waters to the valley, a mysterious force multiplied them threefold, creating abundance ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        where scarcity had reigned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      But this magic would only endure if the River of Return fulfilled its sacred duty. Receivi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        ng the multiplied waters, it had to choose: keep everything for itself, or send back a p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        ortion to replenish the River of Giving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      The first seasons were difficult. When the River of Return hoarded all, the River of Givin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        g ran dry, and both rivers withered. When the River of Giving feared to offer anything, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        the valley remained barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      But when the River of Giving trusted enough to share, and the River of Return honored that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (         trust by giving back generously, both rivers swelled with abundance. The valley bloomed) Tj ET
