BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      # The River of Multiplying) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The people of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        the East were blessed each season with five golden seeds. But these seeds, when thrown i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        nto the river toward the West, would multiply threefold by the time they reached the opp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        osite shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      At first, the Eastern villagers clutched their seeds tightly, fearing loss. The Western vi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        llagers received nothing and grew resentful. Both remained poor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      Then came a wise woman named Hana, who declared: "What good are seeds hoarded in darkness?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (         True wealth flows like water." She cast all five seeds into the river. They became fift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        een by the time they reached the West.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      The Western villagers, moved by this trust, sent back seven seeds through the sacred curre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        nt. Though diminished by the reverse journey, Hana received more than she had given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      Seeing this, both villages learned the river's secret: wealth multiplies only through the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        courage to give and the honor to return. Those who sent little received little back. Tho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        se who trusted much and returned fairly prospered together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      The elders taught: "The river judges not the amount, but the spirit of exchange. Flow crea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        tes abundance; stagnation brings poverty.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      Thus balance was born from trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 39 of 1030) Tj ET
