BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    In ancient times, two villages were separated by a vast desert. Each village had a single we) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ll, but a strange magic bound them: any water poured into one well would triple before flo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      wing into the other village's well.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    The villages took turns as the Giver. When the First Village poured water, it flowed threefo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ld to the Second Village, who then chose how much to send back through the desert directly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (       \(without multiplication\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    At first, fear ruled. The First Village sent little, thinking, "What if they keep it all?" R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      eceiving only a trickle, the Second Village returned nothing. Both grew thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    Then came the season of drought. The First Village's elder said, "We perish either way. Let ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      us pour generously and trust." They sent their full bucket. The Second Village received th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ree buckets-abundance! ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    Grateful and moved by such trust, they sent back two buckets. The First Village now had more) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (       than they started with! The Second Village, having kept one bucket, also thrived.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    From that day forward, both villages prospered. They learned that the magic was not in the w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ells, but in the courage to give freely and the wisdom to return fairly. The desert bloome) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      d, fed by the overflow of their mutual trust.) Tj ET
