BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of Giving and the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      iver of Return. Each was fed by a different mountain spring, and neither alone could bring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (       life to the land.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    The River of Giving was generous but weak, trickling through the dust. When it offered its w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      aters to the valley, a mysterious force multiplied them threefold, creating abundance wher) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      e scarcity had reigned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    But this magic would only endure if the River of Return fulfilled its sacred duty. Receiving) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (       the multiplied waters, it had to choose: keep everything for itself, or send back a porti) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      on to replenish the River of Giving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    The first seasons were difficult. When the River of Return hoarded all, the River of Giving ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ran dry, and both rivers withered. When the River of Giving feared to offer anything, the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      valley remained barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    But when the River of Giving trusted enough to share, and the River of Return honored that t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      rust by giving back generously, both rivers swelled with abundance. The valley bloomed ete) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      rnal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    The ancients learned: prosperity flows not from taking, but from the sacred cycle of giving ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      and returning. Break the cycle, and all thirsts. Honor it, and all flourish.) Tj ET
