BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    # The Tale of the River and the Seeds) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    In the time before time, there lived a farmer named the Giver and a trader named the Keeper.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (       Between them flowed a magical river that tripled whatever passed through its waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    Each season, the Giver received five seeds. She could plant them herself, harvesting five cr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      ops, or trust them to the river. The Giver learned that when she sent seeds downstream, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      e river's magic transformed them into fifteen. The Keeper, receiving this bounty, faced a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      choice: hoard all fifteen, or honor the trust by returning a fair share.) Tj ET
