BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The people of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        the East were blessed each season with five golden seeds. But these seeds, when thrown i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        nto the river toward the West, would multiply threefold by the time they reached the opp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        osite shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      At first, the Eastern villagers clutched their seeds tightly, fearing loss. The Western vi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (        llagers received nothing and grew resentful. Both remained poor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      Then came a wise woman named Hana, who declared: "What good are seeds hoarded in darkness?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (         True wealth flows like water." She cast all five seeds into the river. They became fift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        een by the time they reached the West.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      The Western villagers, moved by this trust, sent back seven seeds through the sacred curre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        nt. Though diminished by the reverse journey, Hana received more than she had given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      Seeing this, both villages learned the river's secret: wealth multiplies only through the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        courage to give and the honor to return. Those who sent little received little back. Tho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        se who trusted much and returned fairly prospered together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
