BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      # The Tale of the River and the Seeds) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      In the time before time, there lived a farmer named the Giver and a trader named the Keepe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        r. Between them flowed a magical river that tripled whatever passed through its waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      Each season, the Giver received five seeds. She could plant them herself, harvesting five ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        crops, or trust them to the river. The Giver learned that when she sent seeds downstream) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        , the river's magic transformed them into fifteen. The Keeper, receiving this bounty, fa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        ced a choice: hoard all fifteen, or honor the trust by returning a fair share.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      In the first years, fear ruled. The Giver sent nothing; the Keeper received nothing. Both ) Tj ET
