BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      Each season, the Giver received five seeds. She could plant them herself, harvesting five ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (        crops, or trust them to the river. The Giver learned that when she sent seeds downstream) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        , the river's magic transformed them into fifteen. The Keeper, receiving this bounty, fa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        ced a choice: hoard all fifteen, or honor the trust by returning a fair share.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      In the first years, fear ruled. The Giver sent nothing; the Keeper received nothing. Both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        starved on their meager five.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      Then came a season when the Giver, desperate, sent all five seeds downstream. The river tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        ipled them, and the Keeper stood before fifteen crops. Remembering his own hunger, he re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        turned eight to the Giver.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      The Giver had eight crops-more than before! The Keeper had seven-also more than his usual ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        five!) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      From that day forward, both prospered. The river taught them: trust is the seed, cooperati) Tj ET
