BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of Giving and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (         River of Return. Each was fed by a different mountain spring, and neither alone could b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        ring life to the land.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      The River of Giving was generous but weak, trickling through the dust. When it offered its) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (         waters to the valley, a mysterious force multiplied them threefold, creating abundance ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        where scarcity had reigned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      But this magic would only endure if the River of Return fulfilled its sacred duty. Receivi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        ng the multiplied waters, it had to choose: keep everything for itself, or send back a p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ortion to replenish the River of Giving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      The first seasons were difficult. When the River of Return hoarded all, the River of Givin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        g ran dry, and both rivers withered. When the River of Giving feared to offer anything, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        the valley remained barren.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      But when the River of Giving trusted enough to share, and the River of Return honored that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (         trust by giving back generously, both rivers swelled with abundance. The valley bloomed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (         eternal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      The ancients learned: prosperity flows not from taking, but from the sacred cycle of givin) Tj ET
