BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      In the time before time, there lived a farmer named the Giver and a trader named the Keepe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        r. Between them flowed a magical river that tripled whatever passed through its waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      Each season, the Giver received five seeds. She could plant them herself, harvesting five ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        crops, or trust them to the river. The Giver learned that when she sent seeds downstream) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        , the river's magic transformed them into fifteen. The Keeper, receiving this bounty, fa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        ced a choice: hoard all fifteen, or honor the trust by returning a fair share.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      In the first years, fear ruled. The Giver sent nothing; the Keeper received nothing. Both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        starved on their meager five.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      Then came a season when the Giver, desperate, sent all five seeds downstream. The river tr) Tj ET
