BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        osite shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      At first, the Eastern villagers clutched their seeds tightly, fearing loss. The Western vi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        llagers received nothing and grew resentful. Both remained poor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      Then came a wise woman named Hana, who declared: "What good are seeds hoarded in darkness?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (         True wealth flows like water." She cast all five seeds into the river. They became fift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        een by the time they reached the West.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      The Western villagers, moved by this trust, sent back seven seeds through the sacred curre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        nt. Though diminished by the reverse journey, Hana received more than she had given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      Seeing this, both villages learned the river's secret: wealth multiplies only through the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        courage to give and the honor to return. Those who sent little received little back. Tho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        se who trusted much and returned fairly prospered together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
